  "name": "Harpie Ladies",
  "category": "curated",
  "format": "classic",
  "manual": "**Game plan:** swarm cheap WIND fliers, pump them with field/equip boosts, and use every Harpie summon to blow up the opponent's backrow — overwhelm through accumulated attack power and spell/trap destruction while controlling their S/T.\n\n**Key cards / engine:** Harpie Lady 1 (+300 to all WIND) + Harpies' Hunting Ground; Elegant Egotist -> Harpie Lady Sisters; Hysteric Party mass-revival.\n\n**How to pilot / combo lines:**\n- **The core swarm loop is Elegant Egotist.** With any \"Harpie Lady\" already up, Egotist Special Summons 1 \"Harpie Lady\" or \"Harpie Lady Sisters\" from your hand or Deck [CDB]. Each Harpie that hits the field triggers `Harpies' Hunting Ground` — destroy 1 Spell/Trap whenever a Harpie Lady/Sisters is Normal or Special Summoned [CDB] — so every summon doubles as 1-for-1 backrow removal.\n- **Stat stacking is real.** `Harpie Lady 1` gives all WIND +300 [CDB]; `Harpies' Hunting Ground` gives all Winged Beasts +200/200 [CDB]; `Cyber Shield` equips a Harpie for +500 [CDB]. A 1300-base Harpie under all three swings for ~2300.\n- **`Harpie's Pet Dragon` scales with the board:** gains 300 ATK/DEF for each Harpie Lady on the field [CDB] — three Harpies make it a 2000+900=2900 boss. Tribute a spent flier into it as your finisher.\n- **Harpie Lady Sisters + Triangle Ecstasy Spark:** Sisters must be Special Summoned by Elegant Egotist [CDB]; once out, `Triangle Ecstasy Spark` makes all Harpie Lady Sisters 2700 ATK, stops the opponent from activating Traps, and negates their Trap effects already on the field [CDB].\n- **`Hysteric Party` is the recursion engine:** discard 1 card to Special Summon as many \"Harpie Lady\" as possible from your GY [CDB]; every revived Harpie re-triggers Hunting Ground. Rebuild an entire board after a Mirror Force.\n- **`Birdface`** adds a Harpie Lady from Deck to hand on battle-death, and **`Flying Kamakiri #1`** Special Summons a WIND monster with ATK <=1500 from Deck on battle-death [CDB] — both refuel the swarm. `Harpie Queen` discards to search Harpies' Hunting Ground [CDB].\n- **`Sonic Shooter`** can attack directly if the opponent's Spell & Trap Zone is empty [CDB] — Hunting Ground clears it for you, so it's a reliable direct hit. `Icarus Attack` tributes a spent Winged Beast to destroy 2 cards.\n\n**Weaknesses:** individual Harpies have low ATK, so a big single beater walls the swarm; the deck folds hard to Torrential Tribute/Mirror Force into an over-committed board; and negating name-treatment shuts off Elegant Egotist.",
